From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sandbox: include <signal.h> before defining SYS_SECCOMP

glibc declares SYS_SECCOMP as an enumerator in <bits/siginfo-consts.h> and
then defines a macro of the same name. This header has an #ifndef guard but
never pulls that in, so when it is processed first the guard sees nothing, the
macro is defined here, and glibc's enumerator later expands to "1 = 1":

  bits/siginfo-consts.h:219:3: error: expected identifier

Include <signal.h> before the guard so glibc's definition wins when present.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/sandbox/linux/system_headers/linux_seccomp.h
+++ b/src/sandbox/linux/system_headers/linux_seccomp.h
@@ -214,6 +214,13 @@
 #define SECCOMP_RET_INVALID 0x00010000U  // Illegal return value
 #endif
 
+// glibc declares SYS_SECCOMP as an enumerator in <bits/siginfo-consts.h> and
+// then defines a macro of the same name. Without pulling that in first, the
+// guard below sees nothing, this header defines SYS_SECCOMP itself, and the
+// glibc enumerator later expands to "1 = 1":
+//   bits/siginfo-consts.h:219:3: error: expected identifier
+#include <signal.h>
+
 #ifndef SYS_SECCOMP
 #define SYS_SECCOMP                   1
 #endif
